---
config:
  theme: base
  htmlLabels: false
  fontFamily: 'Segoe UI, Arial, sans-serif'
  flowchart:
    diagramPadding: 24
    nodeSpacing: 28
    rankSpacing: 46
    padding: 16
    wrappingWidth: 260
  themeCSS: |
    .node rect { rx: 8px; ry: 8px; }
    [data-look="neo"].node rect, [data-look="neo"].node polygon, [data-look="neo"].node path, [data-look="neo"].node circle, [data-look="neo"].node .outer-path { filter: none !important; }
    .edgePath path { stroke-width: 2px; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .edge-animation-slow { animation: none !important; stroke-dasharray: none !important; }
    }
---
%% Regenerate from the repository root with Mermaid CLI 12 (add -p <puppeteer config> where Chrome is not bundled):
%% mmdc -i docs/content-flow.mmd -c docs/content-flow-light.json -o docs/content-flow-light.svg -b '#F3F3F5' -I content-flow-light
%% mmdc -i docs/content-flow.mmd -c docs/content-flow-dark.json -o docs/content-flow-dark.svg -b '#101112' -I content-flow-dark
flowchart TB
  accTitle: How content flows
  accDescr: Five steps. 1, schema types in the repository define the embedded Sanity Studio. 2, editors compose a page from those sections in the Studio. 3, publishing saves the page to the Sanity dataset. 4, a GROQ query reads the published page through the Sanity CDN, cached for 60 seconds; a bundled seed page fills in when no project ID is set or the slug is missing from the dataset. 5, React Server Components render one component per section, as an HTML page and its Markdown version.
  Schema["`**1 · Define**
  section types in src/sanity`"]
  Studio["`**2 · Edit**
  compose a page at /studio`"]
  Dataset[("`**3 · Publish**
  Sanity dataset`")]
  Fetch["`**4 · Fetch**
  GROQ via CDN, cached 60 s`"]
  Seed["Bundled seed page"]
  Render["`**5 · Render**
  one component per section`"]
  Html["HTML page"]
  Markdown["Markdown, llms.txt"]
  Schema define@--> Studio
  Studio publish@--> Dataset
  Dataset fetch@--> Fetch
  Seed fallback@-->|no project ID, or slug missing| Fetch
  Fetch render@--> Render
  Render html@--> Html
  Render md@--> Markdown
  define@{ animation: slow }
  publish@{ animation: slow }
  fetch@{ animation: slow }
  fallback@{ animation: slow }
  render@{ animation: slow }
  html@{ animation: slow }
  md@{ animation: slow }
